2347
01:39:12.940 --> 01:39:17.700
like food at the highest level of the culinary universe.

2348
01:39:17.700 --> 01:39:21.450
But I want to take it back down to boots on the ground

2349
01:39:21.450 --> 01:39:26.450
and remind people that this quest that we're on

2350
01:39:28.860 --> 01:39:32.960
to introduce the plant-based lifestyle to as many people

2351
01:39:32.960 --> 01:39:37.960
as possible is only gonna get so far unless we redress

2352
01:39:38.020 --> 01:39:42.600
the problem of food deserts and access in urban communities

2353
01:39:42.600 --> 01:39:44.510
to healthy plant-based foods, right?

2354
01:39:44.510 --> 01:39:46.630
Like it's one thing to, you know, I'm gonna go

2355
01:39:46.630 --> 01:39:50.960
to 11 Madison Park and drop major coin on this crazy meal,

2356
01:39:50.960 --> 01:39:55.087
but what about the average everyday person who's living in..

2357
01:39:56.040 --> 01:39:56.873
East New York?

2358
01:39:56.873 --> 01:39:57.850
Yeah, exactly.

2359
01:39:57.850 --> 01:39:59.600
And there aren't even grocery stores.

2360
01:39:59.600 --> 01:40:04.300
Let alone any kind of healthy plant-based options.

2361
01:40:04.300 --> 01:40:07.760
Which brings me to the next thing I wanted to share,

2362
01:40:07.760 --> 01:40:10.890
which is my friend, Nil Zacharias, has founded

2363
01:40:10.890 --> 01:40:11.723
this new company.

2364
01:40:11.723 --> 01:40:14.870
He's a CEO of a new venture called Plantega.

2365
01:40:14.870 --> 01:40:18.800
You can check it out online at Eat Plantega.

2366
01:40:18.800 --> 01:40:22.470
And essentially the idea, I love this it's brilliant,

2367
01:40:22.470 --> 01:40:27.470
is creating these basically kiosks, like refrigerated kiosks

2368
01:40:28.430 --> 01:40:31.080
that are stocked with healthy plant-based foods

2369
01:40:31.080 --> 01:40:33.270
that they're placing in bodegas.

2370
01:40:33.270 --> 01:40:34.360
They've started in New York.

2371
01:40:34.360 --> 01:40:36.100
I don't know how many locations they have right now.

2372
01:40:36.100 --> 01:40:38.920
But in bodegas, across New York city,

2373
01:40:38.920 --> 01:40:43.920
they're adding these refrigerated kiosks

2374
01:40:45.930 --> 01:40:48.350
that are just stocked with all kinds of healthy stuff.

2375
01:40:48.350 --> 01:40:52.200
So that they're expanding the availability of healthy,

2376
01:40:52.200 --> 01:40:55.600
affordable options into these food desert neighborhoods.

2377
01:40:55.600 --> 01:40:58.300
And some Bodegas have like a grill oriented

2378
01:40:58.300 --> 01:40:59.950
and they also have like a grill option

2379
01:40:59.950 --> 01:41:00.783
or something like that.

2380
01:41:00.783 --> 01:41:02.707
For some takeaway stuff.

2381
01:41:02.707 --> 01:41:04.690
Oh, was there a grill?

2382
01:41:04.690 --> 01:41:06.220
Maybe it's kind of like Starbucks

2383
01:41:06.220 --> 01:41:07.750
where you pull it out of the fridge

2384
01:41:07.750 --> 01:41:10.020
and they'll grill it up there in the bodega.

2385
01:41:10.020 --> 01:41:13.430
But my understanding is that it's pre-prepared

2386
01:41:13.430 --> 01:41:15.720
like sandwiches and salads and things like that.

2387
01:41:15.720 --> 01:41:16.553
Fantastic.

2388
01:41:16.553 --> 01:41:19.620
And this is just out of the gate, it's brand new.

2389
01:41:19.620 --> 01:41:22.830
But certainly an idea we're celebrating.

2390
01:41:22.830 --> 01:41:26.450
And I think it could go a long way towards really addressing

2391
01:41:26.450 --> 01:41:28.910
this problem of healthy food access

2392
01:41:28.910 --> 01:41:31.750
in underprivileged communities.

2393
01:41:31.750 --> 01:41:35.780
So good on you Nil and let me know how I can support

2394
01:41:35.780 --> 01:41:38.810
this mission and what you guys are trying to achieve.

2395
01:41:38.810 --> 01:41:40.510
And, you know, I just made a brunch,

2396
01:41:40.510 --> 01:41:43.645
a mother's day brunch with beyond meat, breakfast, sausage,

2397
01:41:43.645 --> 01:41:45.890
miyoko's butter and just eggs.

2398
01:41:45.890 --> 01:41:46.723
What do you want a medal?

2399
01:41:46.723 --> 01:41:47.556
No, I'm just saying?

2400
01:41:47.556 --> 01:41:49.540
Those are the three on here that I read.

2401
01:41:49.540 --> 01:41:52.860
Yeah, they partner with miyoko's beyond and just.

2402
01:41:52.860 --> 01:41:54.760
Miyoko's it's fabulous. Yeah.

2403
01:41:54.760 --> 01:41:55.670
So cool.

2404
01:41:55.670 --> 01:41:56.640
Cool.

2405
01:41:56.640 --> 01:41:59.330
Awesome. Should we go to some listener questions?

2406
01:41:59.330 --> 01:42:00.490
I would love that.

2407
01:42:00.490 --> 01:42:02.551
Do it, Is it time to do that?

2408
01:42:02.551 --> 01:42:03.384
It is time.
Okay.

2409
01:42:03.384 --> 01:42:04.217
What do you think would happen

2410
01:42:04.217 --> 01:42:06.740
if we went to a daily show?

2411
01:42:06.740 --> 01:42:07.573
You and me daily?

2412
01:42:07.573 --> 01:42:08.406
Daily.

2413
01:42:08.406 --> 01:42:09.446
I'm available.

2414
01:42:09.446 --> 01:42:12.930
(both laughing)

2415
01:42:12.930 --> 01:42:14.010
Wait, that would have been good on.

2416
01:42:14.010 --> 01:42:15.010
Wait, is that on?

2417
01:42:15.010 --> 01:42:16.000
Is this thing on?

2418
01:42:16.000 --> 01:42:17.590
All right. Are we ready?

2419
01:42:17.590 --> 01:42:18.423
Okay, here we go.

2420
01:42:18.423 --> 01:42:19.400
Greg from Virginia.

2421
01:42:19.400 --> 01:42:20.390
Hey Rich.

2422
01:42:20.390 --> 01:42:23.340
My question is about the topic of money.

2423
01:42:23.340 --> 01:42:26.600
As a child, I was taught that money is a variable

2424
01:42:26.600 --> 01:42:29.960
that has a significant influence on our choices.

2425
01:42:29.960 --> 01:42:31.690
How are you gonna pay for it?

2426
01:42:31.690 --> 01:42:33.300
was my parents' first question

2427
01:42:33.300 --> 01:42:35.730
when I would talk about my dreams.

2428
01:42:35.730 --> 01:42:38.220
In "Finding Ultra" Rich, you share a moment

2429
01:42:38.220 --> 01:42:40.310
when you had left your law practice,

2430
01:42:40.310 --> 01:42:42.430
was waiting to get traction as an author

2431
01:42:42.430 --> 01:42:44.440
and was on the brink of financial ruin.

2432
01:42:44.440 --> 01:42:47.260
How were you able to maintain the pursuit of your dream

2433
01:42:47.260 --> 01:42:50.150
and resist the urge to return to your law practice

2434
01:42:50.150 --> 01:42:52.510
exclusively just to provide for your family?

2435
01:42:52.510 --> 01:42:54.970
How would you advise others to think about money,

2436
01:42:54.970 --> 01:42:57.890
especially if it creates an obstacles to making change?

2437
01:42:57.890 --> 01:43:00.530
I want to thank you guys very much for your valuable insight

2438
01:43:00.530 --> 01:43:04.340
and your podcast, and especially this particular format.

2439
01:43:04.340 --> 01:43:06.370
This interactive format makes it much easier

2440
01:43:06.370 --> 01:43:08.750
and much better to be able to interact.

2441
01:43:08.750 --> 01:43:10.850
Have you guys have a great day, bye.

2442
01:43:10.850 --> 01:43:11.753
Thanks Greg.

2443
01:43:12.890 --> 01:43:13.900
That's a great question.

2444
01:43:13.900 --> 01:43:15.460
I think it's an important question.

2445
01:43:15.460 --> 01:43:17.070
No doubt.

2446
01:43:17.070 --> 01:43:20.460
I want to preface what I'm gonna say,

2447
01:43:20.460 --> 01:43:25.460
by saying that I am not telling anyone what to do

2448
01:43:25.610 --> 01:43:30.610
or not to do, nor am I giving any financial advice

2449
01:43:30.680 --> 01:43:33.380
but I will share a little bit of my experience.

2450
01:43:33.380 --> 01:43:36.330
And I think first of all, I'm with you,

2451
01:43:36.330 --> 01:43:37.923
I grew up in the same way,

2452
01:43:41.810 --> 01:43:45.670
being told, you know, when I would give voice to anything

2453
01:43:45.670 --> 01:43:47.320
aspirational or inspiration, you know,

2454
01:43:47.320 --> 01:43:51.200
sort of aspirational for my life being brought back

2455
01:43:51.200 --> 01:43:56.200
down to earth with a heavy dose of kind of prudent reality.

2456
01:43:57.040 --> 01:44:00.420
So I'm on your wavelength, Greg.

2457
01:44:00.420 --> 01:44:03.811
But what I've come to think, the way I've come to think

2458
01:44:03.811 --> 01:44:08.530
about this is as, when I think about money as this balance

2459
01:44:08.530 --> 01:44:13.190
or this dance between responsibility or prudence

2460
01:44:13.190 --> 01:44:16.230
on the one hand and on the other hand,

2461
01:44:16.230 --> 01:44:19.520
understanding that money is just energy.

2462
01:44:19.520 --> 01:44:22.870
You know, money is of course a variable

2463
01:44:22.870 --> 01:44:25.600
that is going to influence choice.

2464
01:44:25.600 --> 01:44:30.150
But the key, I think first and foremost is understanding

2465
01:44:30.150 --> 01:44:32.700
that we don't live in a zero sum game.

2466
01:44:32.700 --> 01:44:37.160
And that by adopting a mindset of universal abundance

2467
01:44:37.160 --> 01:44:39.760
will help you really get that money

2468
01:44:39.760 --> 01:44:43.460
just like everything else is this wave form, this energy.

2469
01:44:43.460 --> 01:44:48.460
Something that in my experience tends to be less important

2470
01:44:48.940 --> 01:44:50.870
and flow a little bit more freely

2471
01:44:50.870 --> 01:44:54.230
when your life is oriented, not around the pursuit of it

2472
01:44:54.230 --> 01:44:57.483
but rather the pursuit of purpose.

2473
01:44:59.160 --> 01:45:03.320
It is true that, you know, I grew up with parents

2474
01:45:03.320 --> 01:45:06.280
who were hammering a similar message into me

2475
01:45:06.280 --> 01:45:10.520
and I oriented my life around that perspective.

2476
01:45:10.520 --> 01:45:13.610
And I found that in so doing,

2477
01:45:13.610 --> 01:45:15.500
it didn't matter how much money I made.

2478
01:45:15.500 --> 01:45:19.300
I never had any of it because I was so out of alignment

2479
01:45:19.300 --> 01:45:23.360
with a greater sense of purpose that I would compensate

2480
01:45:23.360 --> 01:45:28.360
for that lack of fulfillment by spending whatever I had

2481
01:45:29.290 --> 01:45:30.820
to kind of fill that hole.

2482
01:45:30.820 --> 01:45:32.660
So I was chasing the dragon in a way

2483
01:45:32.660 --> 01:45:34.736
that I was never going to get on top of it.

2484
01:45:34.736 --> 01:45:39.160
And it was only by kind of crashing into a wall

2485
01:45:39.160 --> 01:45:42.350
with all of that and flaming out that I was able

2486
01:45:42.350 --> 01:45:45.490
to reconfigure my relationship to money and I did do it

2487
01:45:45.490 --> 01:45:47.290
through an extended period of hardship

2488
01:45:47.290 --> 01:45:48.710
where we didn't have any.

2489
01:45:48.710 --> 01:45:51.910
And that forced me to get really clear on what my needs were

2490
01:45:51.910 --> 01:45:55.230
and what was most important to me and what my values were.

2491
01:45:55.230 --> 01:45:57.910
And I made a commitment to pursue those values,

2492
01:45:57.910 --> 01:46:01.830
irrespective of any kind of financial reward.

2493
01:46:01.830 --> 01:46:03.630
And I will say there were plenty of moments

2494
01:46:03.630 --> 01:46:07.560
where my faith was tested and if Julie had not had my back

2495
01:46:07.560 --> 01:46:11.640
I very well would have scampered back and tried to get a job

2496
01:46:11.640 --> 01:46:14.120
that would pay the bills because it was very difficult.

2497
01:46:14.120 --> 01:46:17.370
It was emasculating, at times very humiliating.

2498
01:46:17.370 --> 01:46:19.190
Didn't you even have to take some,

2499
01:46:19.190 --> 01:46:23.430
like small kind of law gigs at one point

2500
01:46:23.430 --> 01:46:25.359
when things weren't going well.

2501
01:46:25.359 --> 01:46:27.780
Well, I did, I was sort of practicing law

2502
01:46:27.780 --> 01:46:29.060
as I was writing, "Finding Ultra",

2503
01:46:29.060 --> 01:46:31.720
but when that book came out I was like, I'm not doing,

2504
01:46:31.720 --> 01:46:34.051
I drew a line in the sand and I was like,

2505
01:46:34.051 --> 01:46:34.884
I'm not doing it anymore.

2506
01:46:34.884 --> 01:46:37.030
I'm trusting that this is going to open up the door

2507
01:46:37.030 --> 01:46:38.350
to a new path.

2508
01:46:38.350 --> 01:46:40.031
And it took a long time.

2509
01:46:40.031 --> 01:46:41.856
You know, the phone just didn't rang for a long time.

2510
01:46:41.856 --> 01:46:46.070
There were months where we were scrambling

2511
01:46:46.070 --> 01:46:48.720
like nobody's business and having cars repossessed

2512
01:46:48.720 --> 01:46:50.819
and having our trash bins taken away.

2513
01:46:50.819 --> 01:46:53.150
Being unable to, you know, figure out

2514
01:46:53.150 --> 01:46:55.040
how we were gonna feed the kids that night.

2515
01:46:55.040 --> 01:46:58.203
It was really, really difficult.

2516
01:47:00.020 --> 01:47:04.020
My faith was tremendously tested, Julie, you know,

2517
01:47:04.020 --> 01:47:06.280
I look back on it and I don't know how she had the fortitude

2518
01:47:06.280 --> 01:47:10.810
to like have my back in that period of time, but she did.

2519
01:47:10.810 --> 01:47:13.817
And she would constantly hammer home this idea of like,

2520
01:47:13.817 --> 01:47:15.410
the only way out is forward.

2521
01:47:15.410 --> 01:47:16.710
Like you can't go backwards.

2522
01:47:16.710 --> 01:47:19.370
Like you've come too far, the answers you seek

2523
01:47:19.370 --> 01:47:22.350
are ahead of you and I'm with you and we're together

2524
01:47:22.350 --> 01:47:23.500
and we'll figure it out.

2525
01:47:23.500 --> 01:47:27.390
And money comes and money goes but what's important here

2526
01:47:27.390 --> 01:47:31.360
is you finding your voice and figuring out, you know,

2527
01:47:31.360 --> 01:47:33.350
how you're gonna move forward in the world.

2528
01:47:33.350 --> 01:47:35.350
And that's like a precious gift.

2529
01:47:35.350 --> 01:47:38.080
And you know, I'm here to help you honor that.

2530
01:47:38.080 --> 01:47:40.085
And that takes an extraordinary human being.

2531
01:47:40.085 --> 01:47:40.918
It does.

2532
01:47:40.918 --> 01:47:41.751
It really does that.

2533
01:47:41.751 --> 01:47:42.584
Not the average person.

2534
01:47:42.584 --> 01:47:44.320
It's not like, behind every great man

2535
01:47:44.320 --> 01:47:45.153
there's a great woman.

2536
01:47:45.153 --> 01:47:49.170
Like no, she was like the Jedi, while I was like panicking

2537
01:47:49.170 --> 01:47:50.670
in the corner, you know?

2538
01:47:50.670 --> 01:47:53.943
And so without her, none of this happens.

2539
01:47:55.460 --> 01:47:58.150
But I think because we went without, for such a long period

2540
01:47:58.150 --> 01:48:01.290
of time and we were compelled to like live in the moment

2541
01:48:02.280 --> 01:48:05.510
and it really did reframe my relationship with money.

2542
01:48:05.510 --> 01:48:07.670
And these decisions that I made about how I wanted

2543
01:48:07.670 --> 01:48:11.220
to live my life were decoupled

2544
01:48:11.220 --> 01:48:13.920
from any pursuit of financial gain.

2545
01:48:13.920 --> 01:48:15.200
Like I made that bow down.

2546
01:48:15.200 --> 01:48:17.010
I was like, I don't care.

2547
01:48:17.010 --> 01:48:19.690
This is the way I want to go. This is what makes me happy.

2548
01:48:19.690 --> 01:48:20.750
This is what's fulfilling.

2549
01:48:20.750 --> 01:48:23.960
This is where I see promise and opportunity,

2550
01:48:23.960 --> 01:48:25.980
even if I don't see it right now.

2551
01:48:25.980 --> 01:48:27.360
And it didn't have anything to do

2552
01:48:27.360 --> 01:48:30.900
with financial remuneration.

2553
01:48:30.900 --> 01:48:32.962
So you remove that completely from the equation.

2554
01:48:32.962 --> 01:48:37.962
By like removing that, in some weird spiritual equation,

2555
01:48:38.760 --> 01:48:42.620
I created space for it to come in in a different way.

2556
01:48:42.620 --> 01:48:45.800
And by continuing to trust my instincts

2557
01:48:45.800 --> 01:48:50.800
and follow my curiosity and double down on these values

2558
01:48:53.790 --> 01:48:56.410
as kind of the foundation or the architecture

2559
01:48:56.410 --> 01:48:59.660
for what I do professionally, I'm suddenly,

2560
01:48:59.660 --> 01:49:00.860
you know, it's ridiculous.

2561
01:49:00.860 --> 01:49:02.920
But like, I make way more money now than I ever,

2562
01:49:02.920 --> 01:49:04.360
I never thought I would ever have money.

2563
01:49:04.360 --> 01:49:05.700
Like I just made peace with that.

2564
01:49:05.700 --> 01:49:08.010
I will never have money, that's fine.

2565
01:49:08.010 --> 01:49:10.070
And now I've got all this money.

2566
01:49:10.070 --> 01:49:13.440
Like technically I'm like rich, which is fucking crazy.

2567
01:49:13.440 --> 01:49:14.903
You're rich times two.

2568
01:49:17.550 --> 01:49:18.800
I don't think about it.

2569
01:49:18.800 --> 01:49:21.520
I don't think about how much money is coming in,

2570
01:49:21.520 --> 01:49:24.210
my spending habits haven't really changed.

2571
01:49:24.210 --> 01:49:26.080
I don't really do anything differently.

2572
01:49:26.080 --> 01:49:28.880
Like my whole relationship with money is different.

2573
01:49:28.880 --> 01:49:31.400
Like I just hold it loosely.

2574
01:49:31.400 --> 01:49:33.790
And so I don't know how that's instructive to somebody else.

2575
01:49:33.790 --> 01:49:37.720
Other than to say that if I've discovered anything

2576
01:49:37.720 --> 01:49:42.720
through this journey it's that the key is figuring out

2577
01:49:45.950 --> 01:49:47.803
what gets you excited in the morning.

2578
01:49:49.090 --> 01:49:51.600
And with that, you have this opportunity

2579
01:49:51.600 --> 01:49:54.280
and this responsibility to get clear

2580
01:49:54.280 --> 01:49:59.280
on how to orient, like purpose premised on those values

2581
01:50:04.360 --> 01:50:06.660
and whatever it is that is lighting you up,

2582
01:50:06.660 --> 01:50:09.110
the more that you continue to do it,

2583
01:50:09.110 --> 01:50:11.760
the universe starts to orient around you.

2584
01:50:11.760 --> 01:50:14.680
Like it congeals around you to provide opportunities.

2585
01:50:14.680 --> 01:50:18.700
And I think over time, those opportunities lead to some kind

2586
01:50:18.700 --> 01:50:23.100
of vocational situation that will allow you

2587
01:50:23.100 --> 01:50:24.600
to meet your needs.

2588
01:50:24.600 --> 01:50:25.970
I'm not saying you're going to get rich

2589
01:50:25.970 --> 01:50:28.930
or anything like that, but you will find yourself

2590
01:50:28.930 --> 01:50:31.830
in a situation where work doesn't feel like work.

2591
01:50:31.830 --> 01:50:36.403
Because it's something that you would be doing anyway.

2592
01:50:37.820 --> 01:50:38.840
Does that make sense?

2593
01:50:38.840 --> 01:50:39.673
It does.

2594
01:50:39.673 --> 01:50:40.749
I think it's great.

2595
01:50:40.749 --> 01:50:44.070
And I think Jedi Julie deserves to be an action figure.

2596
01:50:44.070 --> 01:50:45.270
She does.

2597
01:50:45.270 --> 01:50:47.090
We know people who make action figures.

2598
01:50:47.090 --> 01:50:47.923
Yeah.

2599
01:50:47.923 --> 01:50:48.756
She'd be good.

2600
01:50:48.756 --> 01:50:50.820
Yeah, I think the other thing too is,

2601
01:50:50.820 --> 01:50:54.010
you know on that note of here's my dream,

2602
01:50:54.010 --> 01:50:55.280
well, how are you going to pay for it?

2603
01:50:55.280 --> 01:50:57.920
All I can tell you is that every dream that I've realized,

2604
01:50:57.920 --> 01:50:59.580
I couldn't pay for.

2605
01:50:59.580 --> 01:51:01.470
If I set out at the beginning to say, well,

2606
01:51:01.470 --> 01:51:03.280
I have this thing, how am I going to pay for it?

2607
01:51:03.280 --> 01:51:05.450
I never would've gotten out of the gate.

2608
01:51:05.450 --> 01:51:07.740
The thing is you have to just start pursuing it.

2609
01:51:07.740 --> 01:51:10.000
And like I said, the universe arranges itself

2610
01:51:10.000 --> 01:51:12.750
around you to provide the support that you need.

2611
01:51:12.750 --> 01:51:15.000
It might not look like what you would like it to look like.

2612
01:51:15.000 --> 01:51:18.600
And it might not be as much as you would like it to be.

2613
01:51:18.600 --> 01:51:23.010
But generally it allows you to take one more forward step.

2614
01:51:23.010 --> 01:51:23.843
Like, that's it.

2615
01:51:23.843 --> 01:51:25.370
You don't get the blueprint.

2616
01:51:25.370 --> 01:51:27.280
You don't get to see where this is leading

2617
01:51:27.280 --> 01:51:29.020
or how it's all going to play out.

2618
01:51:29.020 --> 01:51:31.060
You just don't get to see the whole picture.

2619
01:51:31.060 --> 01:51:34.930
All you get on the daily is a test.

2620
01:51:34.930 --> 01:51:36.320
Can you take that next step?

2621
01:51:36.320 --> 01:51:37.930
Your faith is tested.

2622
01:51:37.930 --> 01:51:42.930
And I think every time you show up to pass that test

2623
01:51:43.010 --> 01:51:45.100
there's something that happens in the universe

2624
01:51:45.100 --> 01:51:47.610
where it says, okay, he passed that test.

2625
01:51:47.610 --> 01:51:51.370
We'll give them a little, throw them a little loose change.

2626
01:51:51.370 --> 01:51:53.300
See if he can pass the next test.

2627
01:51:53.300 --> 01:51:55.870
And also the conversations around you, including from

2628
01:51:55.870 --> 01:51:59.080
if your parents are around and still not just in your head,

2629
01:51:59.080 --> 01:52:00.563
but in your life.

2630
01:52:01.750 --> 01:52:03.540
Those conversations start to change too.

2631
01:52:03.540 --> 01:52:05.147
But it could take many years, could take five years,

2632
01:52:05.147 --> 01:52:06.550
could take 10 years.

2633
01:52:06.550 --> 01:52:09.270
But the conversations, all of a sudden you'll notice one day

2634
01:52:09.270 --> 01:52:12.330
and it won't be about, you know, can he do it

2635
01:52:12.330 --> 01:52:14.550
or you should get a job or blah, blah, blah.

2636
01:52:14.550 --> 01:52:17.610
It'll be, you know, conversations about pride.

2637
01:52:17.610 --> 01:52:18.900
Like, you know.

2638
01:52:18.900 --> 01:52:23.240
Right, because when you're in it, you cannot expect

2639
01:52:23.240 --> 01:52:25.740
the support of people like that.

2640
01:52:25.740 --> 01:52:26.740
They're just not going to,

2641
01:52:26.740 --> 01:52:29.040
like everybody thought I was insane.

2642
01:52:29.040 --> 01:52:30.763
People were telling Julie like, what's the matter with you?

2643
01:52:30.763 --> 01:52:32.330
You got to divorce this guy.

2644
01:52:32.330 --> 01:52:35.290
Like he's completely lost it.

2645
01:52:35.290 --> 01:52:37.900
So that's the way that it is when you're in the midst of it.

2646
01:52:37.900 --> 01:52:40.210
And that makes it even harder to find your footing

2647
01:52:40.210 --> 01:52:41.650
because you start to question yourself,

2648
01:52:41.650 --> 01:52:42.710
like maybe I am insane.

2649
01:52:42.710 --> 01:52:44.720
Everybody else thinks I'm insane.

2650
01:52:44.720 --> 01:52:46.640
Of course, when it all works out, then it's like,

2651
01:52:46.640 --> 01:52:47.670
oh, we're so proud of you.

2652
01:52:47.670 --> 01:52:50.290
And we saw it all the time and we supported you.

2653
01:52:50.290 --> 01:52:51.810
They forget that they were the one saying,

2654
01:52:51.810 --> 01:52:54.920
how are you going to pay for that thing in the beginning.

2655
01:52:54.920 --> 01:52:56.732
And that's just the way that it's wired.

2656
01:52:56.732 --> 01:52:57.565
That's the way it goes.

2657
01:52:57.565 --> 01:52:58.780
And it's not for everybody.

2658
01:52:58.780 --> 01:53:00.230
Like, it was really hard.

2659
01:53:00.230 --> 01:53:03.210
Like I'm not wishing this journey on people.

2660
01:53:03.210 --> 01:53:05.150
Not everybody is cut out for it.

2661
01:53:05.150 --> 01:53:07.377
If you're happy in your job and you have a profession

2662
01:53:07.377 --> 01:53:10.130
and your goal is to provide for your family

2663
01:53:10.130 --> 01:53:12.090
and have barbecues on the weekends.

2664
01:53:12.090 --> 01:53:13.290
That's great.

2665
01:53:13.290 --> 01:53:15.670
I'm not telling people to quit their job.

2666
01:53:15.670 --> 01:53:17.770
I'm speaking to the person who's got that yearning

2667
01:53:17.770 --> 01:53:20.070
in their soul where they feel like they just can't do it

2668
01:53:20.070 --> 01:53:23.350
one more day and they have this sense or this calling

2669
01:53:23.350 --> 01:53:25.110
that there's something out there.

2670
01:53:25.110 --> 01:53:28.980
And all I'm saying is, listen to that, pay attention to it.

2671
01:53:28.980 --> 01:53:31.230
Try to put a little wind in that sail.

2672
01:53:31.230 --> 01:53:34.160
You know, put a little fertilizer in that soil

2673
01:53:34.160 --> 01:53:37.853
and be open to where it might lead you and pay attention.

2674
01:53:39.040 --> 01:53:41.010
You're talking to Greg from Virginia.

2675
01:53:41.010 --> 01:53:42.515
That's right.

2676
01:53:42.515 --> 01:53:44.420
Thanks for the question, Greg.

2677
01:53:44.420 --> 01:53:46.450
Now we're going to go to the great North.

2678
01:53:46.450 --> 01:53:47.540
Hi, Adam and Rich.

2679
01:53:47.540 --> 01:53:51.110
This is John calling from the North of England.

2680
01:53:51.110 --> 01:53:53.610
So I learned to swim three years ago,

2681
01:53:53.610 --> 01:53:57.922
and this summer I'm doing a swim run that has lakes

2682
01:53:57.922 --> 01:54:01.050
and trail running, and it has a lake crossing in it.

2683
01:54:01.050 --> 01:54:04.600
I don't have any access to lakes to train in

2684
01:54:04.600 --> 01:54:08.218
because they've become too polluted in my neck of the woods.

2685
01:54:08.218 --> 01:54:11.520
But I do have access to the sea and obviously

2686
01:54:11.520 --> 01:54:14.380
it can be really rough or it can be cold.

2687
01:54:14.380 --> 01:54:19.140
So it's kind of warmed up to about 44, 45 Fahrenheit now.

2688
01:54:19.140 --> 01:54:20.800
But I can't do huge distances

2689
01:54:20.800 --> 01:54:23.030
'cause I just get really really cold.

2690
01:54:23.030 --> 01:54:24.897
And if it's too rough, then I just get beaten up

2691
01:54:24.897 --> 01:54:27.200
and I again, can't do huge distances.

2692
01:54:27.200 --> 01:54:29.720
So I also have access to a swimming pool

2693
01:54:29.720 --> 01:54:33.930
and I'm just wondering, how would you kind of navigate

2694
01:54:33.930 --> 01:54:35.230
those two options?

2695
01:54:35.230 --> 01:54:38.821
'Cause neither of them is specific to the swim run I'm doing

2696
01:54:38.821 --> 01:54:39.820
but you know, would you emphasize the pool?

2697
01:54:39.820 --> 01:54:41.750
would you emphasize the sea?

2698
01:54:41.750 --> 01:54:44.710
and which would you use for what?

2699
01:54:44.710 --> 01:54:46.030
Thanks very much. Bye.

2700
01:54:46.030 --> 01:54:49.880
John coming in hot with a vegan swimmer run question.

2701
01:54:49.880 --> 01:54:51.150
My favorite kind of question.

2702
01:54:51.150 --> 01:54:54.747
Yes and with the great accent right out of the North,

2703
01:54:54.747 --> 01:54:55.780
the Northern game of Thrones.

2704
01:54:55.780 --> 01:54:59.030
I don't know how far North in England is John.

2705
01:54:59.030 --> 01:55:00.060
The North.

2706
01:55:00.060 --> 01:55:01.450
Wait is John from the North?

2707
01:55:01.450 --> 01:55:03.670
Yeah. Like John Snow.

2708
01:55:03.670 --> 01:55:04.913
Is this John Snow?

2709
01:55:07.220 --> 01:55:08.390
John Snow is not in England.

2710
01:55:08.390 --> 01:55:11.780
First of all. John Snow just learned to swim,

2711
01:55:11.780 --> 01:55:14.130
to me the best part of this question is he just learned

2712
01:55:14.130 --> 01:55:16.840
to swim three years ago and he's in a swim run.

2713
01:55:16.840 --> 01:55:18.050
I love it.

2714
01:55:18.050 --> 01:55:18.883
That's amazing. I love that.

2715
01:55:18.883 --> 01:55:21.890
Do you want to take a stab at this answer first?

2716
01:55:21.890 --> 01:55:24.520
Well I'll let you talk about the best way to train,

2717
01:55:24.520 --> 01:55:26.230
since I just kind of wing it.

2718
01:55:26.230 --> 01:55:29.310
But I mean, with apologies to Nicholas, I don't wing it,

2719
01:55:29.310 --> 01:55:32.733
I do as I'm told, but I do also wing it to some degree.

2720
01:55:34.810 --> 01:55:36.780
The one thing I would recommend because of your ocean.

2721
01:55:36.780 --> 01:55:38.730
Like for me personally, I like to swim in the ocean.

2722
01:55:38.730 --> 01:55:40.430
I don't swim in pools.

2723
01:55:40.430 --> 01:55:44.100
But since you're new to swimming I would guess like a lot

2724
01:55:44.100 --> 01:55:46.690
of even triathletes that are very good in pools.

2725
01:55:46.690 --> 01:55:49.230
They'd often, the transition to getting into open water

2726
01:55:49.230 --> 01:55:50.530
is a little bit rougher.

2727
01:55:50.530 --> 01:55:52.190
They're not that great or comfortable.

2728
01:55:52.190 --> 01:55:54.560
Let's just say they're not as comfortable in open water.

2729
01:55:54.560 --> 01:55:57.146
And there is a comfort level of swimming in open water

2730
01:55:57.146 --> 01:56:00.230
that you won't have in the, although there will be wind

2731
01:56:00.230 --> 01:56:01.730
in a Lake and there might be waves.

2732
01:56:01.730 --> 01:56:04.161
It won't be the same thing as a rough sea.

2733
01:56:04.161 --> 01:56:07.760
And so if you're going to go into the sea and there's not

2734
01:56:07.760 --> 01:56:10.300
a lifeguard on duty and you're swimming alone,

2735
01:56:10.300 --> 01:56:12.950
I'd be very cautious at first if you're not comfortable

2736
01:56:12.950 --> 01:56:16.470
with it, I would try to swim in tandem at least,

2737
01:56:16.470 --> 01:56:18.790
in the open water, especially at those temperatures

2738
01:56:18.790 --> 01:56:21.500
that's dangerous and it can be dangerous

2739
01:56:21.500 --> 01:56:22.970
if you're not in the right wetsuit.

2740
01:56:22.970 --> 01:56:25.660
And so I think that those things, you know, in Hawaii

2741
01:56:25.660 --> 01:56:27.877
there's a phrase they have on almost every beach,

2742
01:56:27.877 --> 01:56:30.250
"when in doubt don't go out".

2743
01:56:30.250 --> 01:56:32.670
And I think it's okay to feel some butterflies

2744
01:56:32.670 --> 01:56:34.840
but I don't think it's okay to put yourself

2745
01:56:34.840 --> 01:56:36.690
in a dangerous situation.

2746
01:56:36.690 --> 01:56:39.970
So I do think you need to be mindful of conditions

2747
01:56:39.970 --> 01:56:42.100
and temperature if you're gonna be alone.

2748
01:56:42.100 --> 01:56:44.230
And so that's the only thing I would say about the ocean.

2749
01:56:44.230 --> 01:56:46.709
Adam drop-in open water safety knowledge

2750
01:56:46.709 --> 01:56:49.993
like a true lifeguard, a true Waterman.

2751
01:56:52.930 --> 01:56:54.619
So here's what I think.

2752
01:56:54.619 --> 01:56:56.490
I think you're going to be fine.

2753
01:56:56.490 --> 01:56:59.730
John, kudos for tackling a swim run

2754
01:56:59.730 --> 01:57:01.350
three years into learning how to swim.

2755
01:57:01.350 --> 01:57:03.050
I think that's ballsy and amazing.

2756
01:57:04.300 --> 01:57:08.300
If it makes you feel any better, I trained almost entirely

2757
01:57:08.300 --> 01:57:12.090
for the teleswim run world championships in a swimming pool.

2758
01:57:12.090 --> 01:57:13.520
I almost never went and open water.

2759
01:57:13.520 --> 01:57:16.250
Now, that being said, I have a lot of open-water experience.

2760
01:57:16.250 --> 01:57:19.720
So I didn't feel the need to get comfortable on open water.

2761
01:57:19.720 --> 01:57:23.250
So what I would say to you is doubled down

2762
01:57:23.250 --> 01:57:26.640
on the swimming pool, use that as much as possible

2763
01:57:26.640 --> 01:57:30.240
to develop your fitness and your endurance

2764
01:57:30.240 --> 01:57:31.660
and your strength.

2765
01:57:31.660 --> 01:57:35.253
And you can also use the pool for in and out,

2766
01:57:35.253 --> 01:57:36.820
you know, swim run transitions, right?

2767
01:57:36.820 --> 01:57:39.510
So in and out swim, run, swim, run, swim, run

2768
01:57:39.510 --> 01:57:41.230
get used to swimming and running.

2769
01:57:41.230 --> 01:57:43.950
And if you can, if they'll let you at your pool,

2770
01:57:43.950 --> 01:57:46.360
swim in the pool with your wetsuit on and your shoes on

2771
01:57:46.360 --> 01:57:47.560
because swimming with tennis shoes

2772
01:57:47.560 --> 01:57:50.520
is a very strange sensation

2773
01:57:50.520 --> 01:57:52.140
that you're going to have to acclimate to.

2774
01:57:52.140 --> 01:57:55.530
And if the pool allow you to do it

2775
01:57:55.530 --> 01:57:57.310
I would suggest doing that as much as possible.

2776
01:57:57.310 --> 01:57:59.860
And of course, using the hand paddles and getting used

2777
01:57:59.860 --> 01:58:02.930
to all the gear on all of that is really important.

2778
01:58:02.930 --> 01:58:07.930
But I would say that the pool is sub optimal.

2779
01:58:07.940 --> 01:58:09.500
You always want to be kind of out

2780
01:58:09.500 --> 01:58:13.370
in the natural environment, in terrain that's gonna mimic

2781
01:58:13.370 --> 01:58:14.670
the actual race course

2782
01:58:14.670 --> 01:58:16.890
and that isn't quite available to you.

2783
01:58:16.890 --> 01:58:21.890
So what I would suggest is you avail yourself of the sea

2784
01:58:22.260 --> 01:58:25.450
but just pick your moments like once a week

2785
01:58:25.450 --> 01:58:30.450
or when the conditions are, you know, fine.

2786
01:58:30.703 --> 01:58:32.800
Like I wouldn't go out when it's crazy choppy

2787
01:58:32.800 --> 01:58:33.633
or anything like that.

2788
01:58:33.633 --> 01:58:35.860
And also 44, 45 degrees is no joke.

2789
01:58:35.860 --> 01:58:38.350
So make sure you're wearing an appropriate wetsuit

2790
01:58:38.350 --> 01:58:39.600
for that kind of weather.

2791
01:58:40.440 --> 01:58:41.530
Five mil at least.

2792
01:58:41.530 --> 01:58:45.670
Yeah, get out in the sea and you could do short

2793
01:58:45.670 --> 01:58:50.670
swim, run workouts, where you're just, you swim 200 meters

2794
01:58:51.080 --> 01:58:54.240
and then run up the shore and, you know, run for a half mile

2795
01:58:54.240 --> 01:58:56.520
and then go and then run back into the sea.

2796
01:58:56.520 --> 01:58:58.783
So you're not really in the ocean that long

2797
01:58:58.783 --> 01:59:01.710
but you're getting used to, you're acclimating

2798
01:59:01.710 --> 01:59:05.870
